<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cortes of Cádiz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> of Cádiz was the national parliament that met in Cádiz from 1810 to 1814, while most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> was occupied by French forces. Representing Spain and its American territories, it proclaimed national <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and in 1812 adopted the Constitution of Cádiz, a founding text of Spanish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American liberalism. Ferdinand VII annulled its work on his return in 1814.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cortes-of-cadiz.jpg" alt="Cortes of Cádiz" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagihuin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1812SpanishConstitutionMap.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
